(7469342, 1185414, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Wow, does this shot ever remind me of <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=108544" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Magnumphotography</a>...in a good way though!  Great portrait, love the use of bokeh and thirds, lots of contrast and fantastic tones.  Like the contrast of the curving neck vs that huge evil-looking bill. Looks like the light was quite high at the time, so good work on avoiding hard shadows and glare. <br/> <br/>The only reason I can think of for this shot doing poorly, is partly due to the fact that FS is always tough, and simply that there isn''t an unfortunate frog or fish in its bill, or in the act of being tossed down that gullet, with a decorative stream of water trailing behind it.  <br/> <br/>Hope this helps, keep shooting and enetering!<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Wow, does this shot ever remind me of  Magnumphotography...in a good way though!  Great portrait, love the use of bokeh and thirds, lots of contrast and fantastic tones.  Like the contrast of the curving neck vs that huge evil-looking bill. Looks like the light was quite high at the time, so good work on avoiding hard shadows and glare.  The only reason I can think of for this shot doing poorly, is partly due to the fact that FS is always tough, and simply that there isn''t an unfortunate frog or fish in its bill, or in the act of being tossed down that gullet, with a decorative stream of water trailing behind it.   Hope this helps, keep shooting and enetering! Susan', '2016-08-22 08:43:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7469347, 1185701, 100831, '<td valign="top">Wonderful</td>', 'Wonderful', '2016-08-22 09:02:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7469348, 1185818, 100831, '<td valign="top">This gets better with each view, though I should expect that from you.</td>', 'This gets better with each view, though I should expect that from you.', '2016-08-22 09:04:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7469359, 1185553, 63218, '<td valign="top">After thinking about this one, I came back to look again. I''m working on the theory that one of the differences between the thought processes of a photographer and a painter is in the shadows. In general, I think a photographer is more focused on weakening the shadows so that detail is visible. In general, a painter is likely to see shadows as detail &amp; feels no particular impulse to weaken them. So the thing that mainly makes this look like a painting, for me, is the shadows.</td>', 'After thinking about this one, I came back to look again. I''m working on the theory that one of the differences between the thought processes of a photographer and a painter is in the shadows. In general, I think a photographer is more focused on weakening the shadows so that detail is visible. In general, a painter is likely to see shadows as detail & feels no particular impulse to weaken them. So the thing that mainly makes this look like a painting, for me, is the shadows.', '2016-08-22 12:59:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7469362, 1185088, 56502, '<td valign="top">I see sunglasses ;-)</td>', 'I see sunglasses ;-)', '2016-08-22 13:35:45.000000', NULL, 0),
